# Not build inputs. These change often (CI, most docs, and browser-test
# commits), and anything left here invalidates the `COPY . .` layer and with it
# the whole wasm+cargo build. Published Markdown is an exception: Vite renders
# it into the webapp. Root *.md stays: several are read at build time
# (README as the workspace `readme`, CHANGELOG by the webapp version script's
# fallbacks).
#
# This is the only ignore file either image gets. Both builds use the repo root
# as context, and BuildKit reads `<context>/.dockerignore` or a sibling
# `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` - never a `.dockerignore` that merely lives beside
# the image's other sources.
.github
# The webapp build reads every published guide, so these are build inputs. Kept
# per shelf rather than per file: a new guide is published by adding it to its
# folder, and listing files here would be a second place to forget.
docs/*
!docs/usage
!docs/usage/**
!docs/hosting
!docs/hosting/**
!docs/development
!docs/development/**
!docs/legal
!docs/legal/**
packages/rom-weaver-webapp/tests
